      <h2 class="section-title">Three kinds of people keep telling me they have a book.</h2>
      <ul class="list-plain">
        <li><b>The pastor with a sermon series.</b> You preached it. People asked for it. The recordings are sitting on a hard drive. That series is already a book; it just hasn't been typed.</li>
        <li><b>The coach or counselor with a framework.</b> You've walked fifty people through the same process. A book lets the next five hundred find you, and it makes the first meeting shorter.</li>
        <li><b>The believer with a devotional or a testimony.</b> Forty days of what God taught you in a hard season. The story of how He brought you back. You don't need a platform. You need it finished.</li>
      </ul>
