<section class="section-line on-light" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Questions</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">The ones everyone asks.</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Who owns the book?</summary><p>You do. All of it. The manuscript, the files, the cover, the Amazon listing, and every dollar of royalty. It publishes under your own KDP account, which we set up together on a screen-share. I keep nothing but the memory of writing it.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Whose name is on the cover?</summary><p>Yours. Ghostwriters have helped pastors and leaders write books for as long as there have been books. If you'd like "with David S. Jones" on the cover, I'm glad to be there. If you'd rather I stay invisible, that's the normal arrangement and I'm fine with it.</p></details>
      <details><summary>I have nothing written down. Can this still work?</summary><p>Yes. That's what the Drawn Out tier is for. We record three conversations and I write the book from what you said. Most people find they have far more than they thought once someone asks the right questions.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How long does it take?</summary><p>Ninety days from the first call to a live Amazon listing is the plan for a book. A devotional runs shorter. The main thing that slows a project down is a chapter sitting in your inbox unread, so we set review dates on the calendar at the start.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What about a devotional or a study guide?</summary><p>Same process, shorter manuscript. Thirty, forty, or ninety entries, each with a passage, a reflection, a prayer, and a question. Priced on the call, and less than a full book.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How will it sound like me and not like you?</summary><p>Because it starts with you. Your recordings, your sermons, your phrases, the translation you preach from. I build a page of how you actually talk before I write a line, and you read every chapter and mark anything that isn't you. By the third chapter people usually stop finding anything.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you use AI?</summary><p>Yes, the same way I use a word processor and a recorder. It helps me transcribe, organize, and draft faster. It does not decide what the book says. You do, and I do, and every sentence is read by a human who loves the Lord before it reaches you.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What does publishing cost on top of this?</summary><p>Nothing. Amazon KDP is free to publish on, the cover is included, and you buy author copies at print cost if you want them in your hands or on a table at church.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

